{
  "abstract": "Standalone, zero-dependency Lean 4 (v4.36.0) formalization proving an unconditional finite-graph improvement on Balogh–Clemen–Lidický Conjecture 1.4 (European Journal of Combinatorics 121, 2024, Paper No. 103841, arXiv:2203.15764): for every rational density alpha = p/q in [63/100, 1] and every finite simple triangle-free graph G on n >= 100,000 vertices, there exists a vertex subset A of exact size floor(alpha * n) such that e(A) + e(A^c) <= ((2*alpha - 1) / 4) * n^2, with zero + o(n^2) asymptotic error term. This lowers the published threshold from alpha >= 0.717 down to alpha >= 63/100 = 0.63, closing 66.3% of the open conjecture gap [2 - sqrt(2), 0.717]. The proof combines exact integer 2-partition concavity rounding, a vertex-transfer monotonicity lemma, a single rank-2 5x5 integer sum-of-squares certificate verified over all 388/1,024 labeled triangle-free 5-graphs by pure kernel decide, a 3-line global sum-of-squares proof for alpha >= 2 - sqrt(7)/2 (approx 0.6771), and exact 2D/3D homogeneous Bernstein binary-tree certificates (510 leaves, 36 pruned nodes), compiled entirely inside the Lean 4 kernel with zero external dependencies, zero sorry, zero native_decide, and only standard Lean axioms.",
